[2026-07-01T09:27:13.653212] [DEBUG] Parsed tool call: Final Answer params={'content': 'ayo twin 🤙 so i dove into the codebase and the whole "prefub spawner" thing is really just a single file: `PrefabSpawner.cs`. no cap, that\'s the entire infrastructure rn. it\'s a MonoBehaviour you slap on a GameObject, and it handles everything from input, preview, cycling, to actually spawning prefabs in VR.\n\nhere\'s the low-down:\n\n🛠 **core components**\n- **prefabs list** (`List<GameObject> prefabs`) – holds the prefabs you want to spawn. you assign \'em in the inspector.\n- **selectedIndex** – tracks which prefab is currently chosen.\n- **rayOrigin** – transform from where the raycast shoots (probably ur controller/hand).\n- **raycastMaxDistance / defaultSpawnDistance** – max range for raycast; the spawn distance fallback isn\'t used directly (it\'s there for possible future use ig).\n\n🎮 **input handling** (XRI)\n- uses an `InputActionAsset` (the whole asset) and subscribes to ALL actions from all action maps – then filters inside `OnActionPerformed` by map name + control name + action name. \n- **spawn trigger**: right controller\'s "Activate" action with `triggerpressed` → calls `TrySpawnSelected()`.\n- **cycle prefab**: right controller "Haptic Device" action with `secondarybutton` → calls `CycleNext()`. (low-key that\'s a sneaky way to reuse the haptic action for cycling lmao).\n- there\'s also a separate `placementActionRef` (exposed) used just for the placement indicator hold state – it\'s separate from the spawn action.\n\n👀 **placement indicator**\n- in `Update()`, checks if the placement action is pressed. if so, it activates `activeWhileHeldObject` and the `placementIndicator`.\n- the indicator follows the raycast hit point (or default forward distance if nothing hit). rotation aligns to surface normal.\n- so you get a live preview of where the prefab will land, hella useful.\n\n✨ **spawning logic**\n- `TrySpawnSelected()` does a raycast. if it hits something, instantiate the selected prefab at the hit point rotated to the surface normal. returns true/false.\n- won\'t spawn if prefabs list empty or rayOrigin missing. logs warnings.\n- there\'s a legacy `SpawnSelected()` that just calls `TrySpawnSelected()` and ignores the bool – exists for backward compatibility, deadass.\n\n🔄 **cycling**\n- `CycleNext()` increments index, wraps around, logs, updates UI.\n- `CyclePrevious()` decrements similarly, but it\'s never called in the script itself – probably wired up elsewhere or intended for extension.\n\n🎨 **ui indicators**\n- `indicatorObjects` array – all get enabled.\n- `indicatorHighlights` array – only the one at selectedIndex gets enabled, showing which prefab is selected.\n- both are public arrays, so you can drop whatever game objects you want for visual feedback.\n\n🧩 **architecture style**\n- no separate spawn manager or pool – it\'s a straight-up instantiate-based spawner.\n- no object pooling, no lifetime handling, no networking – just simple VR prefab placement.\n- heavily tied to XRI input conventions (right interaction/right maps, triggerpressed, secondarybutton). if the mappings ever change, you\'ll need to adjust the string checks in `OnActionPerformed`.\n- the fact that it subscribes to ALL actions is a bit sus performance-wise, but it works if the action asset isn\'t massive.\n\nso yeah, that\'s the whole prefab spawner infrastructure twin. it\'s clean, gets the job done, but definitely room for expansion if u want pools, undo, network sync, or better input handling. hmu if u need me to map out extension points or find other related scripts fr. periodt 💅✨'}
