[2026-07-01T09:28:10.340892] [DEBUG] Parsed tool call: Final Answer params={'content': "bet, here are all the inputs mapped for the prefab spawner twin:\n\n🎮 **spawn selected prefab**\n- **action map**: `XRI Right Interaction`\n- **action name**: `Activate`\n- **control**: `triggerpressed` (right trigger press)\n- **condition**: must be a button press (`ctx.ReadValueAsButton()`)\n- calls `TrySpawnSelected()` ➔ instantiates the current prefab where the raycast hits.\n\n🔄 **cycle to next prefab**\n- **action map**: `XRI Right`\n- **action name**: `Haptic Device` (ya, they reused the haptic action for cycling, low-key clever)\n- **control**: `secondarybutton` (the B button on right controller, usually)\n- **condition**: button press only\n- calls `CycleNext()` ➔ wraps around the prefabs list.\n\n👆 **placement indicator hold**\n- uses a separate `placementActionRef` (public field, you assign it in inspector).\n- no hardcoded map/action – it just checks `placementAction.IsPressed()` every frame.\n- while held, it shows `activeWhileHeldObject` and the `placementIndicator` (which follows raycast hit).\n\n🧩 **not bound but exists**\n- `CyclePrevious()` – method is there, but nothing in the script calls it. you could wire it up yourself (e.g., secondary button on left controller or double tap).\n\n⚠️ **head's up**\n- the script subscribes to **all** actions from the whole `InputActionAsset` and filters in code. so only those two combos actually do something; everything else just logs `Action performed: ...` for debug.\n- no keyboard or mouse fallback – it's pure XRI controller input rn.\n\nanything else u wanna know about the setup? i gotchu fr 🫡✨"}
